From 516b9f51ef16396b9a3837df1a9c3b2ae824c320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 21:21:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: omci: reconcile services after a MIB reset

930-176 (net: omci: restore ONU-created MEs on MIB reset) rebuilds the
MIB on a MIB Reset - the standard ONU-created defaults and the active
profile's vendor MEs - but omci_agent_mib_reset_locked() never calls
reconcile_services again afterward, even though
omci_agent_clear_services_locked() at the top of that same function
just tore down every applied service.

A MIB Reset is not unusual OLT behavior; it's a normal part of G.988
post-activation provisioning. On a profile whose datapath is default-
seeded MIB state rather than explicit OLT Creates (Nokia/ALCL's VEIP
bridge, for example), that state survives the reset untouched - a
partial reset only erases OLT-origin objects - but nothing reapplies
it to hardware. The ONU is left in O5 with OMCI up and no datapath at
all, indefinitely, until some unrelated event (e.g. an Alloc-ID
assignment) happens to trigger reconcile again.

Reconcile once more after a successful reset so the just-rebuilt MIB
gets re-applied to hardware instead of leaving the ONU stranded.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
 net/omci/agent.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/omci/agent.c b/net/omci/agent.c
index 775d849f94f4..01e2691ba622 100644
--- a/net/omci/agent.c
+++ b/net/omci/agent.c
@@ -2618,6 +2618,19 @@ static int omci_agent_mib_reset_locked(struct omci_device *odev, bool all,
 	agent->upload_index = 0;
 	omci_agent_reset_duplicate_locked(agent);
 
+	/*
+	 * omci_agent_clear_services_locked() above tore down every applied
+	 * service. The MIB objects it left in place (or just rebuilt) may
+	 * still describe a complete datapath - e.g. a profile's default-
+	 * seeded VEIP bridge, which a MIB Reset never touches since it only
+	 * erases OLT-origin objects. Without this, a MIB Reset (which every
+	 * OLT sends as a normal part of post-activation provisioning)
+	 * leaves the ONU in O5 with OMCI up and no datapath, indefinitely,
+	 * until some unrelated event happens to trigger reconcile again.
+	 */
+	if (!ret)
+		omci_agent_reconcile_services_locked(odev);
+
 	return ret ?: reset_ret;
 }
 
